// Description: Detects SMB (TCP 445/139) network connections initiated by Windows Explorer (explorer.exe) to external public IP addresses, which may indicate malicious UNC path execution, phishing-driven file access, or attempted communication with adversary-controlled SMB infrastructure outside the internal network.
// MITRE ATT&CK: T1021.002, T1105, T1204
// Data Sources: DeviceNetworkEvents
// Threat Actor: Commonly associated with phishing campaigns, malware delivery chains, and adversary lateral movement or staging over SMB; not attributed to a single actor.
// Severity: High
// False Positives: Rare legitimate use cases such as sanctioned external SMB services, misconfigured network routing, VPN edge cases, or security testing environments.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where InitiatingProcessFileName =~ "explorer.exe"
| where RemotePort in (445,139)
| where not(ipv4_is_private(RemoteIP))
| project
    Timestamp,
    DeviceName,
    RemoteIP,
    RemotePort,
    InitiatingProcessFileName
